        <mxCell id="108" value="&lt;b&gt;Show advanced settings&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=24;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#1f2937;fontColor=#111827;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="530" y="950" width="330" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="109" value="&lt;b&gt;Calibrate rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. The button is disabled, and the reason is written underneath it, whenever calibrationBlockReason() returns a value: locked, not connected, no reading, warming (with seconds left), sensor fault, signal settling, or over/alarm.&lt;br&gt;2. Setting the baseline writes R0 to the app, records a calibration history entry, audits test.device.calibrated, and sends CAL to the device.&lt;br&gt;3. Advanced sensor settings is collapsed by default and carries the MQ-3 conversion constants. Any signed-in officer can still edit them (KI-10).&lt;br&gt;4. Apply settings and Restore factory defaults are locked while a roadside test is active." style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1f2937;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="500" y="1140" width="390" height="290" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
